Z||000008||Wrench||11-23-2001||06:46 AM||||Be sure to have lots of fluid in the "pressure tank". When ready to flush/bleed the system just slowly stroke the pump and watch the air bubble work it's way up the clear tubing. As soon as the fluid starts to run out of the cap screw it on and start the process. Suggest you put a few rags down to catch the fluid that spills out. This stuff likes to eat paint! Good luck<BR>||||reg||1
